      "teacherReviewRequired": true,
      "markedParagraph": "The husbands of Naomi and Ruth died. When [Naomi] returned to [Israel], her daughter-in-law [Ruth] went with her. To find food, Ruth gathered leftover [grain] in a field belonging to [Boaz]. Boaz was [kind] to Ruth and told his workers to leave [extra] grain for her. Naomi said that Boaz was a [family] protector. She told Ruth to lie near his [feet] at night. Ruth asked Boaz to [marry] her. After he spoke to another relative, they married and had a son named [Obed]. Their family later included King [David]."
    },
